<title>UK: ICO coffee exports reach 82 mln bags in July/June.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports reach 82 mln bags in July/June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Coffee Organization (ICO) said producing members' exports reached 82.08 million 60-kg bags in the 12 months to June 1997, up from 73.18 million in the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>But in June alone, exports fell to 5.87 million bags from 7.03 million in May. Exports in June 1996 totalled 5.88 million bags.</p>
<p>In the first nine months of the current 1996/97 (Oct/Sept) year to June, total exports were up at 63.49 million bags from 56.00 million in the same period in 1995/96.  </p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		     Jun 97    Jun 96  Oct/Jun 96/97   Oct/Jun 95/96</p>
<p>    Brazil	 1,215	 968	14,402	    8,225</p>
<p>    Colombia	 915	 902	 8,828	    8,464</p>
<p>    Guatemala	257	 316	 3,921	    3,256</p>
<p>    El Salvador    134	 115	 2,546	    1,663</p>
<p>    Mexico	   149	 193	 4,131	    4,120</p>
<p>    Indonesia	494	 599	 3,660	    3,730</p>
<p>    Uganda	   291	 194	 3,429	    3,234</p>
<p>    Vietnam	   72	 119	 4,848	    3,377</p>
<p>    Ethiopia	 214	 232	 1,540	    1,235</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast    348	 313	 2,288	    2,135</p>
<p>    Kenya	    124	 179	 1,127	    1,307</p>
<p>    Costa Rica     200	 165	 1,689	    1,786</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
